From 6c1154108fdc63ebab1d0ef7514c7231fbd96ca1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:16:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a run requeued by a gateway restart resumes
 the lost run's conversation

When the run immediately before a Kanban run ended owner_restart_lost (exit 76,
owner_restart), the owner copies that run's persisted active transcript into the
new run's own fresh session before its first turn, and the worker's prompt carries
a resume note plus current card state instead of the 16k-char transcript tail.

Admission/ownership are unchanged: new run id, claim, session id and
owner_admitted marker; the old session is only read. A trailing tool call with no
recorded result gets a synthetic 'interrupted by gateway restart' result. Fallback
to today's tail-only fresh session when the prior session is missing, empty or
unreadable, lives in another home/state.db or profile, or already exceeds the
model's compaction threshold (resolved with the same compression config parser and
ContextCompressor the worker uses). Each such run logs a restart_resume event with
resumed_session_id (also stamped on owner_admitted) or the fallback reason.

Crash, timeout and other requeues are unchanged (tested).
